---
import BackLink from '../components/BackLink.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SOURCE_URL } from '../lib/config';
---

<Layout title="Privacy · Grade Viewer" description="How Grade Viewer handles StudentVUE logins and grades.">
	<main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 pb-16">
		<div class="-ml-1 flex items-center gap-1">
			<BackLink href="/" label="Back" />
			<h1 class="text-xl font-medium">Privacy</h1>
		</div>
		<p class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated August 27, 2026</p>

		<div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">
			<p>
				Grade Viewer is a small educational helper for looking at the grades your school already
				stores in StudentVUE. It is not a district system, and it is not affiliated with,
				endorsed by, or associated with Edupoint, StudentVUE, Synergy, or any school district. It
				is not used for profit, and it is not a place where we collect or keep student grade
				records.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">This app talks to StudentVUE from your browser</h2>
			<p>
				When you sign in, <strong class="font-medium text-foreground">your browser talks to
				StudentVUE over HTTPS</strong>. Grade Viewer’s website does not receive your password,
				gradebook, documents, mail, or attendance. Those stay between this device and your
				school’s StudentVUE system.
			</p>
			<p>
				Browsers block some of those StudentVUE connections, so a small relay forwards the
				encrypted connection to Edupoint hosts. The relay can see that a connection to StudentVUE
				happened. It does not decrypt your login or grades. What-if / hypothetical scores stay on
				this device and are never sent to StudentVUE or to us.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">Usage counts</h2>
			<p>
				We want a rough idea of how many people use Grade Viewer. We do <strong
					class="font-medium text-foreground">not</strong> get your email address, password, or
				grades.
			</p>
			<p>
				Instead, your browser turns your email into a one-way ID, then sends us only that ID. We
				store the ID and the time you signed in so we can count unique users. Nobody (including
				us) can turn that ID back into your email. Sign-in needs this step to finish. Later visits
				may refresh the last-seen time for the same ID.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">What we store</h2>
			<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
				<li>A hashed usage ID and last sign-in time, for counts only.</li>
				<li>Normal website hosting logs (someone visited the site). We do not use those logs to
					identify students.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">What we don’t keep</h2>
			<ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
				<li>We do not create StudentVUE accounts or keep a database of grades.</li>
				<li>We do not get your password, email, gradebook, documents, mail, or attendance on our
					servers—only the hashed usage ID above.</li>
				<li>We do not sell, share, or look through your gradebook, documents, mail, or attendance.</li>
				<li>We do not send what-if scores back to StudentVUE or to anyone else.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">What stays on your device</h2>
			<p>
				After you sign in, this browser can save an encrypted copy of your StudentVUE login so you
				don’t have to type your password again. The encryption key stays on this device and cannot
				be copied off it. Remember Me keeps that login across visits; without it, it lasts for this
				browser session. Signing out deletes the saved login.
			</p>
			<p>
				This browser may also keep a local gradebook snapshot so pages load faster, plus mail,
				documents, and attendance for this tab. Signing out clears those copies. What-if edits live
				only in this tab until you leave the course page. A theme choice and a profile-picture
				preference can stay in this browser even after you sign out.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">What goes back to StudentVUE</h2>
			<p>
				What-if scores are local only. Mail actions you take here—marking a message read, deleting
				it, or moving it—are sent to StudentVUE, the same as in the official app. Grade Viewer does
				not change the grades your school has on file.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">Who actually has your grades</h2>
			<p>
				Your school and StudentVUE (Edupoint) already have your grades. Their privacy rules still
				apply. Grade Viewer only shows what StudentVUE returns when you sign in from this browser.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">Terms of use</h2>
			<p>
				By signing in, you agree to these terms. Grade Viewer is an independent educational
				project. It is not affiliated with Edupoint Educational Systems, StudentVUE, Synergy, or
				any school district. Those names and marks belong to their owners.
			</p>
			<p>
				This site is for educational purposes only. It is not used for profit: no ads, paid plans,
				or sale of student data. Use it only with your own StudentVUE account, and follow your
				district’s rules.
			</p>
			<p>
				The app is provided “as is,” without warranties. Grades here may be incomplete or out of
				date compared with StudentVUE. Grade Viewer and its operators are not liable for missed
				work, wrong displayed grades, account problems, school action, or any other loss from
				using this tool. You use it at your own risk.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">Open source</h2>
			<p>
				Grade Viewer is open source. You can read the code at
				{' '}<a class="underline" href={SOURCE_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{SOURCE_URL.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">Hosting</h2>
			<p>
				Someone has to host the website so you can open it. That host serves the app pages and
				receives the hashed usage ID above. It does not get your StudentVUE password, email, or
				grades. A small relay helps the browser reach StudentVUE; it sees that an encrypted
				connection happened, not the contents of your login or grades.
			</p>

			<h2 class="text-base font-medium text-foreground">Questions</h2>
			<p>
				If you did not mean to use this tool, sign out. That clears the saved login and the local
				grade, mail, document, and attendance copies on this device. You can also close the tab. We
				may keep the hashed ID and last sign-in time for counts only. We do not keep your password
				or gradebook.
			</p>
			<p>
				For feedback, problems, or other questions, email
				{' '}<a class="underline" href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</main>
</Layout>
